{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q222936","formula":"C₄H₇NO","hill":"C4H7NO","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":4.0,"H":7.0,"N":1.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"Acetone cyanohydrin","ru":"Ацетонциангидрин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Acetone cyanohydrin (ACH) is an organic compound with the formula (CH3)2C(OH)CN. It is a colorless liquid used in the production of methyl methacrylate, the monomer of the transparent plastic polymethyl methacrylate (PMMA), also known as acrylic. It liberates hydrogen cyanide easily, so it is used as a source of such. For this reason, this cyanohydrin is also highly toxic.","ru":"Ацетонциангидри́н — органическое вещество, простейший циангидрин. Широко используется в химической промышленности для получения метилметакрилата — сырья (мономера) для получения полиметилметакрилата («органического стекла»)."},"fame":20,"pubchemCid":6406,"mass":85.1,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(C)(C#N)O","inchikey":"MWFMGBPGAXYFAR-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-hydroxy-2-methylpropanenitrile","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"6406","atoms":13,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.858,"y":-0.001,"z":1.375,"el":"O"},{"x":2.2,"y":0.0,"z":-0.041,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.432,"y":0.0,"z":0.012,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.976,"y":1.258,"z":-0.663,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.974,"y":-1.258,"z":-0.665,"el":"C"},{"x":1.04,"y":0.001,"z":-0.018,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.07,"y":1.292,"z":-0.601,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.608,"y":2.165,"z":-0.167,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.686,"y":1.311,"z":-1.719,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.069,"y":-1.287,"z":-0.613,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.616,"y":-2.162,"z":-0.158,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.674,"y":-1.317,"z":-1.717,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.563,"y":0.829,"z":1.787,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,2,1],[0,12,1],[1,5,3],[2,3,1],[2,4,1],[2,5,1],[3,6,1],[3,7,1],[3,8,1],[4,9,1],[4,10,1],[4,11,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wi